    "IFC 070 FlexPower"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (battery-powered electromagnetic water flowmeter)",
  "applies_to": "IFC 070 electronic revision 5.1.0, Modbus version 1.1.1 (battery) and 1.1.0 (FlexPower), per AD IFC 070 Modbus R02.",
  "summary": "The IFC 070 is KROHNE's battery-powered electromagnetic water meter converter, with an optional mains (FlexPower) supply and an RS-485 Modbus RTU add-on. Flow, totalizers, pressure and temperature are offered three times: as doubles, floats and integers. This map covers the double and float banks, the integer litre counters, alarms, coil commands and the Modbus settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The tables list the Modbus protocol (data) address, which goes on the wire unchanged: flow speed at 3000 is requested as 3000. In a 1-based or Modicon tool add 1 (3001 / 43001)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Electronic revision 5.1.0; Modbus 1.1.1 (battery) / 1.1.0 (FlexPower)",
  "source": {
    "title": "IFC 070 Supplementary Instructions - Battery powered electromagnetic water meter with optional FlexPower",
    "doc_number": "4005415902 - AD IFC 070 Modbus R02 en",
    "revision_date": "2022-05",
    "url": "https://core.instrumart.com/assets/krohne-ifc-070-v3-signal-converter-supplementary-instructions.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "technical data p. 4; local configuration p. 6; addressing and functions p. 9; coils pp. 10-12; registers pp. 13-19; Modbus settings p. 25; system information p. 26; diagnostics p. 27; data encoding p. 31"
  },
  "notes": [
    "This copy is hosted by the distributor Instrumart; it is KROHNE document 4005415902 (AD IFC 070 Modbus R02).",
    "Word order: the data-format setting (8004) offers little endian, big endian (default) and two mixed-endian modes, and the data encoding page says the most significant byte of any multi-byte quantity is sent first. In the default big-endian mode, 32- and 64-bit values are therefore ABCD (highest word first). If the data format is changed, the order changes too.",
    "The register banks can be read with function 03 or 04 and written with 16; coils with 01/02 and 05. The register section says every address can be read with any function code, so the coil addresses also read as unsigned integers.",
    "Left out: integer-format flow speed (5000), pressure (5014), temperature (5016, 5032) and battery capacity (5026/5028), because the manual gives no scaling for these integer values; the measurement-settings block 6000-6027, whose printed layout is too jumbled to tie each code to its address; and the string/array identity registers other than the serial numbers.",
    "Settings registers marked R/W* only accept writes after unlocking with the access-control register 9998 and with the special write option enabled; changes are held until 'Apply changes' (coil 1002).",
    "To save battery the Modbus interface can be switched off when mains power is lost (default off) and can be set to listen only at a reception interval."
  ],
